## 1. Project Overview

### What This Project Does

CREST Automation is an **API vs Database validation framework** that verifies the correctness of a financial portfolio management application. It does this by making live API calls and independently querying the PostgreSQL database, then comparing results to ensure they match within defined thresholds.

### Business Purpose

In a financial application, even minor discrepancies between the data the backend computes and what the API serves to the frontend can lead to incorrect portfolio valuations, misleading analytics, and loss of user trust. This framework automates the detection of such discrepancies across:

- **Portfolio wealth summaries** (Total Wealth, Asset Allocation, Cash & Equivalent)
- **Holdings counts** (Equity, MF, ETF, NPS, FD, RD, Bank Deposits)
- **Historical performance** (at multiple past dates)
- **Risk analysis** (Risk Concentration, Contributors, Geography Allocation)
- **Family aggregation** (consolidated view across all family members)
- **Manage-assets** (including manually added assets)

### Why API vs DB Validation Matters

| Risk Without Validation | What This Framework Catches |
|---|---|
| Backend bug silently returns wrong total | Grand total mismatch > 0.25% threshold |
| New asset class missing from aggregation | Holdings count mismatch (exact match) |
| Family ID treated as User ID in SQL | Incorrect 0 values returned |
| Historical snapshot returning live data | Date-filtered SQL vs date-parameterized API |
| Unit conversion errors (Cr/L/K) | Pre-normalized comparison logic |

