### Authentication Flow Detail

```
auth.setup.js
    │
    ├─ new AuthAPI()
    ├─ POST {BASE_URL}/auth/v1/signup
    │     body: { phone_number, full_name, recaptcha_token }
    │
    ├─ POST {BASE_URL}/auth/v1/verify-otp
    │     body: { phone_number, otp }
    │     response: { access_token }
    │
    └─ Write .auth/token.json → { accessToken: "eyJ..." }
         also: process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN = token

Per test → fixtures.js
    │
    ├─ Read process.env.ACCESS_TOKEN  (fast path)
    │   OR fs.readFileSync('.auth/token.json')
    │
    └─ new APIClient(accessToken)
         All requests: Authorization: Bearer {accessToken}
```

**Key point:** Authentication happens **once per run**, regardless of how many tests execute.

